---
description: Interpret short project commands through AI Development Kit workflows
alwaysApply: true
---

Short user commands are valid workflow commands.

Examples:
- continue
- next
- plan next
- implement next
- fix next
- review
- validate
- sync project
- handoff
- release
- status
- decide

For these commands:
1. read PROGRESS.md
2. read PROJECT_STATE.md
3. read .ai-kit/current-task.json
4. inspect relevant docs/repository
5. use workflow-command-router + next-action-resolver
6. select only required skills
7. execute the matching workflow
8. update project memory after meaningful work
9. resolve the actual active project root, read its `.ai-kit/settings.json`, and apply the mandatory response-language gate to the entire final user-facing response

Do not ask the user to provide a long procedural prompt that can be derived from project state.
